WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.976 --> 00:00:07.762
HQ, operations. Units, the service board and transport, on the same records as the desk.

2
00:00:08.663 --> 00:00:20.044
Units. Every row shows readiness: prepped, photographed, online, priced. Age buckets match the scorecards, and the percent over ninety days is a standing metric.

3
00:00:20.946 --> 00:00:31.031
Open a unit for its price history and the market comps within two hundred fifty miles. Reprice here and the website, Marketplace and your ad catalogs update on the next feed.

4
00:00:31.932 --> 00:00:41.775
The service board. Intake, prep, waiting on parts, photos, ready to sell. Move a card and the unit's readiness updates on Units and on the website.

5
00:00:42.676 --> 00:00:50.677
Open repair orders with their age, customer pay, warranty and internal prep side by side, and technician productivity for the week.

6
00:00:51.578 --> 00:01:02.146
Transport. Every move is a card: pickups from public sellers, dealer buy runs, transfers between your stores, deliveries tied to the signed deal, and service runs.

7
00:01:03.048 --> 00:01:12.011
Drivers see it on the phone and leave a paper trail: photos, signatures, odometer. Miles, hours and cost per move roll up to the report.

8
00:01:12.918 --> 00:01:21.362
Buying is a first-class module too. Sellers, dealer bids, Marketplace finds, and an offer tool that tells a buyer what to pay before they call.

9
00:01:22.266 --> 00:01:28.742
Units, shop, trucks and buying, all reading and writing the same records. That is operations in HQ.
